  "id": "ex-07-verben-praepositionen-a2",
  "intro": "Standalone drill set, not tied to any lesson. Many German verbs pair with a fixed preposition whose meaning you can't guess (warten AUF, denken AN, sich freuen AUF for something ahead vs. ÜBER for something that already happened). To ask or refer back to a THING, use a wo-/da-compound (worauf/darauf, woran/daran, worüber/darüber). For a PERSON, never use these compounds — use preposition + wen/wem in the question and preposition + pronoun in the answer (auf wen? — auf ihn). Blocks: A Basistraining → B Vertiefung → C Sprachbausteine → D Wiederholung. Answers in solutions.md.\n",
  "lesson": "EX/07-verben-praepositionen-a2",
  "level": "A2",
  "summary": null,
  "title": "Verben mit fester Präposition: warten auf, sich freuen, denken an … — A2",
